     "explanation": "Selective inability to recognize faces, with object recognition spared, is prosopagnosia — typically tied to the fusiform face area and right occipitotemporal cortex. Reliance on voice and gait is the classic compensation. Apperceptive agnosia affects all object perception, not faces selectively; anomia is a naming deficit (the patient still recognizes); neglect is a spatial-attention disorder. Dr. P had prosopagnosia as part of a broader visual agnosia.",
