     "explanation": "Because the music was perceived as external and real — she hunted for its source — it was a true musical hallucination, here arising from temporal-lobe seizure activity triggered by her stroke. An earworm is recognized as internal/imagined and easily dismissed; a delusion is a false belief, not a perceptual experience; tinnitus is non-musical ringing. The temporal lobe's role in storing and generating music explains why a focal seizure can replay forgotten songs with hallucinatory vividness.",
