     "explanation": "Penfield's stimulation studies showed that activating temporal-lobe points evoked detailed 'experiential' phenomena — hearing an orchestra, a remembered scene replayed with sensory richness, surges of déjà vu and emotion. This established the temporal lobe as a seat of experiential memory and a generator of perception when abnormally active — exactly what produced Mrs. O'C.'s hallucinated childhood songs. Movement control is frontal/motor cortex, memory is not stored in the cerebellum, and experiential seizures need not convulse.",
